1
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:36,000
My Octopus Teacher is a documentary film directed by James Reed.

2
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:06,000
After years of swimming every day in the freezing ocean at the tip of Africa, Craig Foster
meets an unlikely teacher: a young octopus who displays remarkable curiosity.

3
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Visiting her den and tracking her movements for months on end he eventually wins the animal’s
trust and they develop a never-before-seen bond between human and wild animal.

4
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Self, played by Craig Foster.

5
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Self, played by Tom Foster.

6
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
My Octopus Teacher is a 2020 Netflix Original documentary
film directed by Pippa Ehrlich and James Reed.

7
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
It documents a year spent by filmmaker Craig Foster forging a relationship
with a wild common octopus in a South African kelp forest.

8
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The film won Best Documentary Feature at the 93rd Academy Awards.

9
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The film explores themes of diving, octopus,
intelligence, atlantic ocean, south africa.
